Aurora hardware stack metapackage. Per-device firmware is extracted on the target Mac.

aurora-platform-core carries only the hardware services (update-m1n1,
dracut-asahi, asahi-fwupdate, speakersafetyd, speakerguardd, aurora-audio,
alsa-ucm-conf-aurora and aurora-camera-denoise). It installs no kernel or
boot chain, replaces the Fedora Asahi metapackages and is protected from
removal by dnf.
aurora-platform adds the Aurora kernel, boot chain and release identity.

Performance in tuned-ppd uses aurora-performance (schedutil, kernel boost
policy), avoiding the stock performance governor's idle CPU frequency floor.
Only the stock ppd.conf performance mapping is migrated; custom mappings and
Power Saver are preserved. See docs/power-profiles.md in the source repository
for upgrade handling, qualification and rollback.

Wake for network access follows the power adapter, as on macOS laptops:
magic-packet wake is armed on wired interfaces and Wi-Fi phys that support it
while on AC and disarmed on battery (63-aurora-wake-for-network.rules). Put
"always" or "never" in /etc/aurora/wake-for-network to override.
